    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **257 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreCountsNamesakes`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same firstName and lastName, case-insensitively \u2014 as a read-only computed field on the owner-create endpoint (`POST /api/owners`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes the count against all existing owners *before* the new owner is persisted, via a new helper `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)` that matches both names with `equalsIgnoreCase`, and sets it on the owner.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `namesakeCount` (`Integer`) field mapped to a new `namesake_count` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` by name, so it's returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `namesakeCount` as a `readOnly` `int32` property on the `Owner` schema, which regenerates the `OwnerDto` field.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\nThe value is persisted at creation time (a snapshot), matching the spec's \"before this create\" semantics and the existing pattern used for `customerCode`/`householdId`.",
